WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.361
Two relay switches each store a non-negative integer as 31 binary toggles. To turn the pattern of a

2
00:00:05.361 --> 00:00:10.796
into the pattern of b, a technician flips toggles one at a time. Return how many toggles must

3
00:00:10.796 --> 00:00:13.986
be flipped, which is the number of bit positions where a and b differ.

4
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.485
1 is 001 and 4 is 100; they differ in two positions.

5
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.899
Identical patterns need no flips.

6
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.907
XOR marks every differing position with a 1 bit.

7
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.725
Compute x = a ^ b and repeatedly clear its lowest set bit with x &amp;= x -

8
00:00:40.725 --> 00:00:42.438
1, counting iterations.

9
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.496
XOR leaves a 1 wherever the bits differ, so the answer is the popcount of a ^ b.

10
00:00:48.496 --> 00:00:54.841
Clearing the lowest set bit with x &amp; (x - 1) runs once per set bit. Many languages

11
00:00:54.841 --> 00:00:56.973
also expose popcount as a built-in.

12
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.834
1 ^ 4 = 5 (101).

13
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.419
5 &amp; 4 = 4, count 1; 4 &amp; 3 = 0, count 2.

14
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.663
O(number of differing bits). O(1)
